# This package ships ONE artefact: an upstream Chromium build, unpacked. Every
# tag below is a property of that binary, not a packaging decision, and none of
# them can be resolved without building Chromium from source — which is not a
# thing this project can carry. Ubuntu 26.04 offers no Chromium .deb to depend
# on instead (the archive's chromium-* packages are transitional shims for the
# snap, and a confined snap cannot read the renderer's working directories
# under /var/lib/carlos-emr). See debian/copyright for the licensing, and
# debian/chromium.pin for the exact revision and its checksums.

# Chromium statically links its own copies of these. That is upstream's build
# configuration; the distribution copies are not interchangeable with the
# versions Chromium was tested and shipped against.
embedded-library

# Deliberately not stripped. debian/rules skips dh_strip for this package
# because the binary is vendored rather than built here: stripping a prebuilt
# Chromium discards the symbols its own crash handler needs, and would make any
# renderer crash report unusable. The size cost is accepted for that reason.
unstripped-binary-or-object
